// Title: HackTool - SharpChisel Execution
// Sigma ID: cf93e05e-d798-4d9e-b522-b0248dc61eaf
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-05 | Modified: 2023-02-13
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1090.001
// Description: Detects usage of the Sharp Chisel via the commandline arguments
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://github.com/shantanu561993/SharpChisel
//   - https://www.sentinelone.com/labs/wading-through-muddy-waters-recent-activity-of-an-iranian-state-sponsored-threat-actor/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_sharp_chisel.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\SharpChisel.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoProductName =~ "SharpChisel"
